.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "2024-01-01" "libmyutils" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B int wordCount(FILE* file, int* lines, int* words, int* chars);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wordCount
reads through the file pointed to by
.I file
and counts the number of lines, words, and characters.
.PP
The results are stored in the integer pointers
.IR lines ,
.IR words ,
and
.IR chars .
.PP
Returns 0 on success and -1 on failure (e.g., if file is NULL).
